Cloaky is free for everyone to download and use. We plan to open-source it
once it has found its feet; until then, these are the terms. "Cloaky" here
means the Cloaky app and the parts of it we made: its code, design,
documentation, name, logo and icons. "We" means the Cloaky contributors.

What you can do

- Download, install and use Cloaky for free, on as many machines as you
  like, for personal or commercial work.
- Copy it onto your own and your organisation's machines, and keep backups.
- Keep everything you make with it. Your code and your work are yours.
- Tell people about Cloaky and point them to where we publish it.

What we ask you not to do

- Redistribute, sell, rent or sublicense Cloaky or a modified version of
  it, or offer either to others as a hosted service. Send people to our
  downloads instead.
- Rebrand Cloaky, or pass off Cloaky or a modified version of it as your own.
- Use Cloaky's code or design to build a copy of it or a product that
  imitates it.
- Use the Cloaky name, logo or icons, except to talk about Cloaky itself.

If you have access to Cloaky's source code, you may read, build and change
it for your own use or to contribute to Cloaky, and the points above still
apply.

These permissions last as long as you follow these terms.

